<article class="env-lemma" id="06LM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06LM">Lemma <span data-tag="06LM">15.46.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. The following are equivalent: $R$ is Cohen-Macaulay, the henselization $R^ h$ of $R$ is Cohen-Macaulay, and the strict henselization $R^{sh}$ of $R$ is Cohen-Macaulay. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/06LJ" data-tag="06LJ">15.46.3</a> we know that $R^ h$ and $R^{sh}$ are Noetherian, hence the lemma makes sense. Since we have $\text{depth}(R) = \text{depth}(R^ h) = \text{depth}(R^{sh})$ and $\dim (R) = \dim (R^ h) = \dim (R^{sh})$ by Lemmas <a href="/tag/06LL" data-tag="06LL">15.46.8</a> and <a href="/tag/06LK" data-tag="06LK">15.46.7</a> we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>